[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-79372"] :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ that satisfies $y(1)=e.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}(\\frac{1+x}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{x+1} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1-\\frac{1}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =\\frac{K{e}^{x}}{x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=e$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =e \\\\ \\frac{K{e}^{1}}{1+1} & =e \\\\ K & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=e$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{x+1}\\,.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79425/selection/b4124fd48bb41365000d981efeb801a8652edafc299c74764d26d93ccdbbdc7e" :answer/id #uuid "024eeaad-af55-5751-84c8-a041b7337058" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{3}={e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79425/selection/6aeb37d76f0b2750279ee2aa732d130b8cf282fe1e87032ee39ee9a59df9606b" :answer/id #uuid "727c76bb-14cb-5a53-83e6-bad976b7c23d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=2{e}^{x}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79425/selection/500e7e82dfb1a3f4588518b1808167069e7d9adef95f884ecd308071c1cfb1f3" :answer/id #uuid "89d02a14-92d3-5033-a057-9bd1ad6769e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=3{e}^{x}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79425/selection/6a72d8a5615f09651e2dbfd95567f460c861ae9723fef6fd1eadedbd12e41ee5" :answer/id #uuid "c9561dd3-9d79-5ea4-b343-de193f957c34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79425/selection/96d7d7fbb6dcb305b0052ff61e5cc3c7fa88621cc941474d512a5644ee452646" :answer/id #uuid "05fe0008-1fb0-5e91-98a0-60bf44c51f4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2{e}^{{x}^{2}}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79425/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cddc7849-107c-5824-b5d6-93695259dd65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79425/selection/6a72d8a5615f09651e2dbfd95567f460c861ae9723fef6fd1eadedbd12e41ee5" :answer-field/choices ["q-79425/selection/b4124fd48bb41365000d981efeb801a8652edafc299c74764d26d93ccdbbdc7e" "q-79425/selection/6aeb37d76f0b2750279ee2aa732d130b8cf282fe1e87032ee39ee9a59df9606b" "q-79425/selection/500e7e82dfb1a3f4588518b1808167069e7d9adef95f884ecd308071c1cfb1f3" "q-79425/selection/6a72d8a5615f09651e2dbfd95567f460c861ae9723fef6fd1eadedbd12e41ee5" "q-79425/selection/96d7d7fbb6dcb305b0052ff61e5cc3c7fa88621cc941474d512a5644ee452646"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79425" :question/id #uuid "02d23995-f689-5881-b3ec-6224edc19266" :question/math-academy-id "q-79425" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$  Assume that $y>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3} & =4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x(2+{y}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the left-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=2+{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{2+{y}^{3}}(3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3}) & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}} \\\\ 2+{y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}^{3} & =K{e}^{{0}^{2}}-2 \\\\ 1 & =K-2 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79425/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104059/selection/31a99863f5aaa1391619d2798568ec4e3353bcdb50a5e723f395d8fff60d7888" :answer/id #uuid "9a755514-92bb-506a-8775-2d1708304b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104059/selection/5ccdb6ed52f7f763286370a0bbf3701d85850acab56beac75b58f6b45db10234" :answer/id #uuid "c027f59a-7575-5547-8e1a-bc2ccbcccf58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{x}{1+x+{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104059/selection/67c170eb3c988733cf7b3328429d5e4713e3d157d78d6e526ef40e957f0b38cb" :answer/id #uuid "cf27878b-c87e-50bf-a22a-f8c50efcdbc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104059/selection/1a4d8e11af7fd6409ad3cb465fb4b49a8be31937529e0916b2bf05051b4bb66c" :answer/id #uuid "d948bac9-62a7-5665-95df-522f8b717271" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{2x+{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104059/selection/f855782afecf9042fd4d67a2b03ff76250620e41e739e2afc79fb4c0180db06c" :answer/id #uuid "b5984bc1-4d99-5874-a48a-f57bbe65a914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{2+2x-{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104059/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "42ce8856-c1f6-5ff7-bc9a-c230fc99d9dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104059/selection/67c170eb3c988733cf7b3328429d5e4713e3d157d78d6e526ef40e957f0b38cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-104059/selection/31a99863f5aaa1391619d2798568ec4e3353bcdb50a5e723f395d8fff60d7888" "q-104059/selection/5ccdb6ed52f7f763286370a0bbf3701d85850acab56beac75b58f6b45db10234" "q-104059/selection/67c170eb3c988733cf7b3328429d5e4713e3d157d78d6e526ef40e957f0b38cb" "q-104059/selection/1a4d8e11af7fd6409ad3cb465fb4b49a8be31937529e0916b2bf05051b4bb66c" "q-104059/selection/f855782afecf9042fd4d67a2b03ff76250620e41e739e2afc79fb4c0180db06c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104059" :question/id #uuid "919dc14f-ff69-5952-b9d3-1351ffc6437d" :question/math-academy-id "q-104059" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(-1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+x+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(-1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{1-(-1)^{2}-C(-1)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{C} & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}\\,.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104059/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104059"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347853/field-1/742e9a499e7d94ddc0080956931cae9c418e6ba76fcd7dc0d484d5a5b1ccef42" :answer/id #uuid "0a8eb70a-e41b-5bb2-8a1c-c2d892adb8b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{4x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347853/field-1/ab71760260b8991f25f2e5fc90cbcf89f96c9bdbc0d56a8f683954b5b284c89a" :answer/id #uuid "782f563b-2517-5b65-b3d1-0639cd3da9d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{2x+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347853/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d39f3ea-9301-57f8-ab08-d613b890416e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347853/field-1/742e9a499e7d94ddc0080956931cae9c418e6ba76fcd7dc0d484d5a5b1ccef42" :answer-field/choices ["q-347853/field-1/742e9a499e7d94ddc0080956931cae9c418e6ba76fcd7dc0d484d5a5b1ccef42" "q-347853/field-1/ab71760260b8991f25f2e5fc90cbcf89f96c9bdbc0d56a8f683954b5b284c89a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347853" :question/id #uuid "2221490e-f21a-588c-b91a-30cee47bc521" :question/math-academy-id "q-347853" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2}=0$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(0)=2.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =2x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{1}{2x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{1}{2(0)+C} \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{2}{4x+1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-347853/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347853"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-355525/field-1/f2799c5a31cd3c0fe6ff36761f622527f4d87d715fb2050123d3edbba0f7de2a" :answer/id #uuid "4103ec85-0df0-5ba8-8d38-0644036eed9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}\\cos(4x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355525/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ecc2147-d9e9-5bbb-baa5-a19422b1e77b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355525/field-1/f2799c5a31cd3c0fe6ff36761f622527f4d87d715fb2050123d3edbba0f7de2a" :answer-field/choices ["q-355525/field-1/f2799c5a31cd3c0fe6ff36761f622527f4d87d715fb2050123d3edbba0f7de2a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355525" :question/id #uuid "90c059c9-cfbc-5121-8811-b73c677022f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-355525" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y){y}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=0$ that satisfies $y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=0.$ Assume that $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})+C \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ 0 & =0+C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-355525/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355525"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
